    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44682" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπαρα-κόμιστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to steer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν γῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Luc.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ὁ πλοῦς ἐπὶ τὰ στενά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.44.6
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <i>easy to bring over</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λογισμῷ πρὸς τὸ συμφέρον εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.597b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις] εὐ. πρὸς τὰς παραπομπὰς τῆς ὕλης</span>
			<i>conveniently situated for the supply</i> of wood, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1327a10
			</span></i>.</div>
